        "original_id": "35ae8a64-5c3e-51f7-bf4d-59b6d4251316",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Albert Gallatin\n- Works: The Probability Broach\n- Places: Gallatin Universe, North American Confederacy, Gallatin National Forest\n- Organizations: Democratic-Republican Party\n- Roles: U.S. Secretary of the Treasury\n- Concepts: alternate history, libertarian society\n\nFacts:\n- Albert Gallatin was born on January 29, 1761, and died on August 12, 1849.\n- Albert Gallatin was a Swiss-American politician, diplomat, ethnologist, and linguist.\n- Albert Gallatin was an important leader of the Democratic-Republican Party and served in various federal elective and appointed positions across four decades.\n- Albert Gallatin was U.S. Secretary of the Treasury and a scholar of Native American languages and cultures.\n- Gallatin National Forest is named after Albert Gallatin.\n- The Probability Broach is set in an alternate history called the Gallatin Universe.\n- In The Probability Broach, the Gallatin Universe features a libertarian society on the North American continent called the North American Confederacy (NAC).",
